{
  "about": [
    "Cross-implementation test vectors for wirebond's engine: what the Go implementation, the reference, writes and how it receives (SPEC §7).",
    "Written by the Go implementation's core/vectors_test.go, removed after 382cb8d (git show 382cb8d:core/vectors_test.go), and fixed since; checked against the Rust engine by crates/core/tests/vectors.rs.",
    "Bytes are lowercase hex, times (at) nanoseconds of the session's monotonic clock, flows FlowID numbers (port << 16 | the client's flow number).",
    "Probes are not pinned: the Rust port adds a challenge token to them (notes/open.md R2-03)."
  ],
